# 20. Cross-Screen Context Preservation

This is one of the most important architectural rules in AEGIS.

When the user moves between screens, the system must preserve the active operational context.

The user should never feel:

> "I went to another page and lost the event."

Instead:

> "I changed perspectives on the same event."

## Persistent Operational Context

When applicable, the following context travels with the user:

```text
Active Event
Event Status
Threat Identity
Risk State
Investigation State
Selected Case
Transmission Context
Containment State
Response State
Recovery State
Evidence Context
Confidence / Uncertainty
Relevant timestamps
```

The interface may display different subsets of this information depending on the screen.

