# 23. Human-in-the-Loop Architecture

The operational loop is:

```text
SYSTEM OBSERVES
       ↓
SYSTEM ANALYZES
       ↓
SYSTEM SURFACES
       ↓
HUMAN REVIEWS
       ↓
HUMAN DECIDES
       ↓
SYSTEM RECORDS
       ↓
SYSTEM MONITORS
       ↓
SYSTEM FEEDS BACK
```

For high-consequence actions:

```text
Recommendation
      ↓
Review
      ↓
Authorization
      ↓
Execution
      ↓
Verification
```

The UI must make these stages visually distinguishable.

---

# 24. Uncertainty Architecture

AEGIS must preserve uncertainty throughout the journey.

At any point the system may contain:

```text
Known
Unknown
Suspected
Inferred
Confirmed
Conflicting
Pending
```

These states must not be collapsed into a single "truth" representation.

## Example

Bad:

```text
Transmission source: Ward 3
```

when the evidence only suggests it.

Better:

```text
Potential transmission source
Ward 3
Confidence: [state]
Evidence: [state]
```

The exact confidence model belongs to the domain/state architecture and must not be fabricated inside the UX layer.

