# 33. Action Confirmation Architecture

High-consequence actions require explicit distinction between:

```text
VIEW
```

```text
RECOMMEND
```

```text
PREPARE
```

```text
AUTHORIZE
```

```text
EXECUTE
```

```text
VERIFY
```

This should be reflected in both the state model and UI interaction model.

A button should never obscure whether the user is:

- requesting an action
- approving an action
- executing an action
- recording an action

